# The local service, asked the questions the ADE asks it (T12.7, LLD §13.9).
#
# > flows … over the HTTP adapter against the local service, with JSON-path
# > expectations
#
# Every assertion here is pattern 19's `Wait for the "<name>" API to answer
# "<path>" to …`, which Draft 2.15 added. That is not decoration: the sentence
# was written *because* the self suite needed to say things about a service's
# answer, and a flow that used a capture and a guard instead would be saying the
# same thing in two steps and asserting it in neither.
#
# ## What is deliberately not asserted
#
# The run history. `/runs` is whatever is in `evals/fixtures/runs`, which git
# does not carry, so a clean checkout has none — and a check that reads better
# on the machine that happens to have run something is not a check.

story: the service says it is alive, and which project it is serving
  Wait for the "health" API to answer "$.ok" to be "true"
  Wait for the "health" API to answer "$.project" to contain "evals/fixtures"

story: the service describes the project the ADE would open
  Wait for the "project" API to answer "$.config.project" to be "svatah-fixtures"
  Wait for the "project" API to answer "$.config.adapter" to be "playwright"
  Wait for the "project" API to answer "$.root" to contain "evals/fixtures"

story: the service compiles the project and answers with the plan
  Wait for the "plan" API to answer "$.project" to be "svatah-fixtures"
  Wait for the "plan" API to answer "$.schemaVersion" to be "1.0.0"
  Wait for the "plan" API to answer "$.stories.0.name" to be "book a slot"
  Wait for the "plan" API to answer "$.stories.0.steps.0.action" to be "click"

story: the service reads the bindings store the Bindings screen shows
  Wait for the "bindings" API to answer "$.0.id" to be "app.bookings-link"
  Wait for the "bindings" API to answer "$.0.file" to contain "bindings/app/bookings-link.yaml"

story: the service names every secret and values none of them
  Wait for the "data" API to answer "$.values.user.email" to be "connected2atul@gmail.com"
  Wait for the "data" API to answer "$.secrets.0" to be "user.password"
  Wait for the "data" API to answer "$.values.user.password" to contain "redacted"
  Wait for the "data" API to answer "$.secretSources['user.password'].reads" to be "SVATAH_SAMPLE_PASSWORD"

# The fixtures project exposes no story as a tool, and the answer says so as two
# empty lists rather than as an absence — which is the difference between "no
# tools" and "the route did not answer".
story: the service says which stories an agent may call
  Wait for the "tools" API to answer "$.tools.tools" to be "[]"
  Wait for the "tools" API to answer "$.tools.refused" to be "[]"
  Call the "tools" API

story: the service publishes the description its clients are generated from
  Wait for the "openapi" API to answer "$.openapi" to contain "3."
  Wait for the "openapi" API to answer "$.paths['/health'].get.summary" to contain "Liveness"

# The one route that must *refuse*.
#
# Bound to loopback is not the same as safe: anything on the machine can reach
# 127.0.0.1, so every route but `/health` and `/openapi.json` needs the bearer
# token the service printed when it started (LLD §13.5). This request carries no
# `authorization` header, and what it must get back is a refusal with a sentence
# in it rather than a project.
story: the service refuses a request with no token, and says why
  Wait for the "unauthorised" API to answer "$.error" to be "unauthorised"
  Wait for the "unauthorised" API to answer "$.message" to contain "bearer token"

test: the local service over the HTTP adapter
  the service says it is alive, and which project it is serving
  the service describes the project the ADE would open
  the service compiles the project and answers with the plan
  the service reads the bindings store the Bindings screen shows
  the service names every secret and values none of them
  the service says which stories an agent may call
  the service publishes the description its clients are generated from
  the service refuses a request with no token, and says why
